> C342-13 Hangup can cause loss of objects being moved internally.
I always thought this referred to the mythical gold duplication bug by
forcing a hangup while selling stuff. However, you really can avoid
effects corresponding to messages not already printed if using the tty
port. For example, dig a hole through the floor with a pick-axe, and
hang up after "you dig ..." and before "you fall through". The save
will have you sitting over the hole. Another example, force a hangup
while turning to stone in the two terminal turns where you normally
only get to read messages. On loading, you get 12 movement points,
which you can use to quaff acid etc. Back to the original bug, what
happens if you hangup between "foo hurls a potion of paralysis" and
"crash! something seems to be holding you?"

> C343-46 Breaking up a boulder or statue can result in pieces that are
> described incorrectly.
Total mass is not preserved, in case that matters.

> C343-48 Killing your pet doesn't get you any experience when it should.
Somebody posted you never get experience for killing your steed. Is
that true?

> C343-62 Riding into a magic portal gives an extra, useless message.
Finally, the devteam realizes verbosity is a bug from a software
usability point of view.

> C343-66 Co-aligned unicorns in a bones file may be hostile.
Why is this hard to reproduce?

> C343-68 Incorrect message may be given when a spellcasting monster
> summons other monsters.
Wasn't it a pluralization issue if extinction lets only one of the
monsters materialize?

> C343-78 Digging in an existing hole charges you for the time it takes to
> dig the whole hole.
Dig down with a pick-axe while sitting on a hole (not pit). The game
still charges you the time to dig through a pit. You get onto the hole
in the first place by randomly not falling in, or with a hangup save.


Hope that helps.


